--   **`rowUC_of`**: uniform row additions (label dimension `m`, exponent `τ`) over any Lemma 12
--   table `tab` with a canonical fine Lemma 12 code `l12`.
--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `Solutions.R6IL2Row`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem IntMul.Kappa.R6.IL2.rowUC_of (hm : 16 ≤ m) (hm' : m ≤ 1000000) (hτ0 : 0 ≤ τ) (hτ1 : τ ≤ 1)
--       (hL : L12Canon tab l12 τ) : RowUCP m τ tab
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** Round six, item language (I2): `RowUC`, uniform row additions for any `m`, `τ` and Lemma 12 table
--
--   `RowUC m τ Isym tbl rowC Kc` is the frozen `KFW.RowU` (`KFWRowIface`) with the label dimension
--   `mC = 100^3` replaced by `m` and `τ50 = 1 - 2^-50` by `τ`: the single fixed code `rowC` implements
--   the row addition `Pm i j` on the bits `Fin m × Fin (m^k)` laid out at `posR m K e k`, parameters
--   `[m^k, K, e, t, S0, B, r, H, i, j]` in the background registers `36 … 45`, at cost
--   `≤ (Kc (K+2) + 1) · n · (r (H+1) (m^k + 1)^τ + PsiR r Z H)`.
--
--   `RowUCP m τ tab`: a fixed list of procedures and a code with `RowUC` in every extension
--   `IL.kTableP tab ext`.
--
--   **`rowUC_of`**: `16 ≤ m ≤ 10^6 → 0 ≤ τ ≤ 1 → IL.L12Canon tab l12 τ → RowUCP m τ tab`
--   (code `(rowCodeU l12).ren id (gL E)`, no extra procedures).
